WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:01.820
Z-ARC...

00:00:03.090 --> 00:00:04.220
Z-ARC...

00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:05.440
Z-ARC?

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:06.420
Z-ARC...

00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:06.910
Z-ARC.

00:00:06.910 --> 00:00:07.520
Z-ARC...

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:08.480
Z-ARC?

00:00:14.470 --> 00:00:17.000
No!

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:23.440
Implementing mass into Solid Vision 
has created Action Duels.

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:28.120
In duels where the field, monsters 
and duelists become one,

00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:31.260
the people are caught in a frenzy of excitement!

00:02:05.170 --> 00:02:09.980
The Supreme King's Soul

00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:14.490
I am Z-ARC... The devil duelist.

00:02:14.490 --> 00:02:17.480
With these hands, I tried to...

00:02:18.530 --> 00:02:20.450
You aren't a devil!

00:02:20.980 --> 00:02:23.360
Respond, Yuya! To how everyone feels!

00:02:24.020 --> 00:02:26.460
That's right. When that happened...

00:02:27.270 --> 00:02:28.890
I've made up my mind.

00:02:28.890 --> 00:02:30.900
I won't be a devil anymore!

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:33.800
Now! Do it, Layra!

00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:35.820
Where's Yuzu? Where's Layra?

00:02:35.820 --> 00:02:37.900
Layra is here.

00:02:41.310 --> 00:02:42.880
That child is Layra?

00:02:42.880 --> 00:02:43.710
What?

00:02:43.710 --> 00:02:45.880
No way. Why is he a baby?

00:02:46.320 --> 00:02:49.370
The four spell cards my father made—

00:02:49.370 --> 00:02:54.220
En Flowers, En Birds, 
En Winds, and En Moon—

00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:57.690
had not only the power to separate 
and destroy the dragons

00:02:57.690 --> 00:02:59.520
that made up the Supreme King,

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:03.800
but to purify the dragons' controller 
and the cards' activator.

00:03:03.800 --> 00:03:07.400
In other words, the power 
to return them to infancy.

00:03:07.880 --> 00:03:10.490
That's why, after the former Z-ARC

00:03:10.490 --> 00:03:15.270
split the dimensions, he was 
reincarnated as a baby into each.

00:03:16.170 --> 00:03:19.240
At the same time, my older sister, Ray,

00:03:19.240 --> 00:03:21.550
was also reincarnated as four babies.

00:03:21.910 --> 00:03:22.980
Yuzu...

00:03:23.520 --> 00:03:28.730
But this time, Layra peeled 
the evil heart out of you,

00:03:28.730 --> 00:03:30.490
and absorbed it into himself.

00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:33.320
Does that mean Yuya...

00:03:33.320 --> 00:03:35.230
...is no longer Z-ARC?

00:03:36.700 --> 00:03:38.510
Does that mean Layra...

00:03:38.510 --> 00:03:40.870
...saved Yuya?

00:03:40.870 --> 00:03:43.500
It isn't anything so simple.

00:03:44.460 --> 00:03:49.670
The world, which had begun 
to fuse within ARC-V,

00:03:49.670 --> 00:03:55.410
was ripped into four by their dragons, 
returning it to four dimensions.

00:03:56.370 --> 00:03:59.180
I believe the reason Layra 
was not split into four

00:03:59.180 --> 00:04:03.700
is because he sealed Z-ARC's soul so quickly.

00:04:03.700 --> 00:04:06.520
However, as a result, Layra...

00:04:06.850 --> 00:04:09.530
...has lost his smile.

00:04:10.150 --> 00:04:11.860
Lost his smile?

00:04:11.860 --> 00:04:16.840
There is a reason that I decided to 
restart the Maiami Championship.

00:04:16.840 --> 00:04:20.310
In the hope that Yuya Sakaki's 
entertainment duel

00:04:20.310 --> 00:04:22.940
would restore Layra's smile.

00:04:22.940 --> 00:04:24.520
My entertainment duel?

00:04:24.520 --> 00:04:25.540
Yes.

00:04:25.540 --> 00:04:29.500
With it, you will save not 
only Layra, but the world.

00:04:29.500 --> 00:04:30.990
What are you talking about?

00:04:30.990 --> 00:04:33.790
How will making Layra smile save the world?!

00:04:34.710 --> 00:04:36.840
I am inside Layra.

00:04:36.840 --> 00:04:39.920
My... Z-ARC's evil heart!

00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:43.850
If Layra lost his smile because of that,

00:04:43.850 --> 00:04:45.860
then, if I make him smile again,

00:04:45.860 --> 00:04:49.100
that evil heart will disappear?

00:04:49.100 --> 00:04:50.550
That's right.

00:04:51.060 --> 00:04:53.870
But it isn't as simple as that.

00:04:53.870 --> 00:04:55.400
Well, obviously not...

00:04:55.400 --> 00:04:59.710
Z-ARC is a devil who tried to 
destroy the world, after all.

00:05:00.010 --> 00:05:01.980
Even still, we must try.

00:05:01.980 --> 00:05:05.120
If we cannot, one day, Z-ARC will revive.

00:05:05.120 --> 00:05:07.820
And the world will be endangered once more.

00:05:08.470 --> 00:05:11.900
My entertainment... My evil heart...

00:05:12.660 --> 00:05:14.300
But how?

00:05:15.030 --> 00:05:18.130
The answer lies inside you.

00:05:18.550 --> 00:05:19.460
Dad?

00:05:19.460 --> 00:05:20.570
Sir!

00:05:20.570 --> 00:05:21.770
Darling!

00:05:21.770 --> 00:05:23.830
If you want to find it,

00:05:23.830 --> 00:05:27.910
you must first win this Junior 
Youth Championship.

00:05:28.240 --> 00:05:31.200
If you cannot, you cannot become a pro.

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:34.380
You cannot save Layra and 
Yuzu, let alone the world.

00:05:34.380 --> 00:05:35.150
Yuzu!

00:05:35.440 --> 00:05:36.310
Yuzu!

00:05:37.800 --> 00:05:39.800
You mean that Yuzu is around here?

00:05:39.800 --> 00:05:41.720
My entertainment can save her?!

00:05:42.030 --> 00:05:45.150
I believe that Yuzu Hiiragi is safe.

00:05:45.150 --> 00:05:47.820
Whether she can be saved is up to you.

00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:50.600
Up to him?

00:05:50.600 --> 00:05:53.100
Sure we can put our hopes on him?

00:05:53.650 --> 00:05:56.800
They said he abandoned his evil heart, but...

00:05:58.530 --> 00:05:59.800
Ma'am?

00:06:02.740 --> 00:06:04.880
What's taking you so long, Yuya?!

00:06:05.400 --> 00:06:06.910
Y-Yoko?

00:06:06.910 --> 00:06:11.120
If you have time to stew about it, 
go keep your promise already!

00:06:11.490 --> 00:06:12.580
Mom?

00:06:12.980 --> 00:06:14.190
You said it, right?

00:06:14.190 --> 00:06:17.130
That you'd use your duel 
to make everyone smile,

00:06:17.130 --> 00:06:20.490
stop the war, and bring Yuzu back?

00:06:20.490 --> 00:06:23.930
You haven't kept a single one 
of those promises yet.

00:06:23.930 --> 00:06:25.700
The seeds of war remain,

00:06:25.700 --> 00:06:28.360
there's a baby who's forgotten how to smile,

00:06:28.360 --> 00:06:30.100
and Yuzu isn't back yet!

00:06:30.100 --> 00:06:31.980
Shut up, Mom!

00:06:32.890 --> 00:06:35.120
This is my problem.

00:06:35.120 --> 00:06:38.310
My... My turn!

00:06:40.320 --> 00:06:47.590
I switch Odd-Eyes Pendulum Dragon 
and Hip Hippo to defense position.

00:06:51.520 --> 00:06:55.350
Then, I set one card and end my turn.

00:06:56.600 --> 00:06:59.300
I want to save her, too...

00:06:59.300 --> 00:07:01.470
But how do I do that?!

00:07:05.270 --> 00:07:07.640
Guess my help wasn't required.

00:07:10.840 --> 00:07:11.840
Yoko?

00:07:13.680 --> 00:07:15.320
"Shut up," huh?

00:07:15.800 --> 00:07:19.620
When did he get such a big mouth on him?

00:07:21.080 --> 00:07:23.590
If you're just going sit there 
and beat yourself up,

00:07:23.590 --> 00:07:27.960
then I, the man Gongenzaka, 
will save both Yuzu and Layra!

00:07:27.960 --> 00:07:29.190
My turn!

00:07:29.590 --> 00:07:34.200
I summon Tuner Monster Superheavy 
Samurai Fist from my hand!

00:07:37.600 --> 00:07:40.070
Gongenzaka, summoning in attack position?

00:07:40.070 --> 00:07:44.710
Battle... I attack Hip Hippo with Fist!

00:07:52.120 --> 00:07:56.860
And then, Big Benkei attacks 
Odd-Eyes Pendulum Dragon!

00:07:57.150 --> 00:08:00.060
Big Benkei can attack from defense position.

00:08:04.730 --> 00:08:09.600
In that instant, the effect of Soulhorns, 
equipped to Big Benkei, activates!

00:08:09.880 --> 00:08:13.050
When I have no spells or 
traps in my graveyard,

00:08:13.050 --> 00:08:15.470
its equipped monster can attack twice.

00:08:15.470 --> 00:08:19.310
Go, Big Benkei! Attack Yuya directly!

00:08:31.290 --> 00:08:32.890
Action Spell Evasion!

00:08:33.460 --> 00:08:35.230
I negate the attack!

00:08:35.230 --> 00:08:36.650
You won't escape!

00:08:36.650 --> 00:08:40.530
When Fist destroys a monster by battle,

00:08:40.530 --> 00:08:44.270
I can Synchro Summon during the Battle Phase!

00:08:44.270 --> 00:08:48.060
Level 2 Fist tunes Level 8 Big Benkei

00:08:48.060 --> 00:08:49.970
and Level 2 Superheavy Samurai Preparation!

00:08:51.710 --> 00:08:55.040
Immovable demon, 
steel yourself with determination,

00:08:55.040 --> 00:08:58.450
and become an iron devil 
to traverse the battlefield!

00:08:58.450 --> 00:08:59.920
Synchro Summon!

00:09:00.390 --> 00:09:01.390
Take the field!

00:09:01.690 --> 00:09:07.060
Appear, Level 12 Superheavy 
Samurai Steam Train King!

00:09:09.400 --> 00:09:11.360
A new Gongenzaka monster?

00:09:13.560 --> 00:09:15.120
He's riding on top of it!

00:09:15.530 --> 00:09:19.610
This is the manifestation of my 
preparation, my determination.

00:09:19.610 --> 00:09:22.480
I will defeat you and become a pro.

00:09:22.480 --> 00:09:23.870
Let's go, Yuya!

00:09:23.870 --> 00:09:26.880
I attack you directly with Steam Train King!

00:09:30.050 --> 00:09:31.880
It's running!

00:09:32.200 --> 00:09:35.720
If you've abandoned your desire to 
be a pro, then get out of my way!

00:09:37.860 --> 00:09:40.830
Steam Train King can attack 
in defense position.

00:09:46.430 --> 00:09:48.270
Action Spell Evasion!

00:09:48.270 --> 00:09:49.470
I won't let you!

00:09:52.540 --> 00:09:53.640
He's fast!

00:09:53.640 --> 00:09:55.010
Gongenzaka just...

00:09:55.010 --> 00:09:57.390
Action Spell No Action!

00:09:57.390 --> 00:09:59.210
This negates Evasion!

00:09:59.210 --> 00:10:01.450
Great job, Gongenzaka!

00:10:01.450 --> 00:10:04.320
He tossed off his iron sandals 
to surpass his limitations!

00:10:10.320 --> 00:10:13.160
I activate my trap Performapal Signal!

00:10:15.280 --> 00:10:17.160
I draw one card and send it to my graveyard.

00:10:17.530 --> 00:10:21.270
If it's a Performapal, I can 
negate one of your attacks!

00:10:21.270 --> 00:10:23.760
Oh? He's gambling.

00:10:23.760 --> 00:10:28.170
But if it's a spell, or a trap, 
or just a Normal Monster card,

00:10:28.490 --> 00:10:29.850
Yuya loses.

00:10:30.810 --> 00:10:32.140
Draw!

00:10:34.210 --> 00:10:35.110
Okay.

00:10:35.110 --> 00:10:38.650
I send Performapal Swordfish 
to the graveyard.

00:10:38.650 --> 00:10:41.290
That negates Steam Train King's attack!

00:10:46.120 --> 00:10:47.590
It stopped!

00:10:47.590 --> 00:10:49.040
What?!

00:10:50.900 --> 00:10:53.500
I activate Steam Train King's effect!

00:10:53.500 --> 00:10:58.400
Once per turn, I can banish all spells 
and traps from my graveyard,

00:10:58.400 --> 00:11:01.640
and for each, I deal you 
200 points of damage.

00:11:01.950 --> 00:11:02.600
What?

00:11:02.600 --> 00:11:05.980
I banish Action Spell No Action 
from my graveyard!

00:11:06.320 --> 00:11:09.130
Take 200 points of damage!

00:11:13.080 --> 00:11:14.380
It gives me shivers!

00:11:14.380 --> 00:11:16.190
This is so exciting!

00:11:16.640 --> 00:11:19.520
I never thought I'd see an 
Action Card back-and-forth

00:11:19.520 --> 00:11:22.290
in a duel between Yuya and Gongenzaka!

00:11:25.030 --> 00:11:28.130
It's truly a pulse-pounding development.

00:11:28.130 --> 00:11:32.780
Gongenzaka, who pledged to fight immovable 
duels, attacked from atop a monster!

00:11:32.780 --> 00:11:37.180
And to stop it, entertainment duelist 
Yuya bet everything on one draw.

00:11:37.180 --> 00:11:39.580
Further, Gongenzaka dealt damage,

00:11:39.580 --> 00:11:43.780
using a monster effect and Action Card combo!

00:11:45.320 --> 00:11:47.440
You've gotten soft, Yuya!

00:11:47.440 --> 00:11:50.290
Thinking you can become a 
pro this way is ridiculous!

00:11:50.290 --> 00:11:51.600
What did you say?

00:11:51.600 --> 00:11:53.490
It's your turn next.

00:11:53.490 --> 00:11:56.000
If you really want to become a pro...

00:11:56.000 --> 00:11:59.240
If you want to be an entertainment 
duelist, like your father...

00:11:59.240 --> 00:12:02.370
You'd better come at me with 
everything you have.

00:12:02.370 --> 00:12:04.570
I am doing everything I can!

00:12:04.570 --> 00:12:06.400
I'm thinking as hard as I can...

00:12:06.400 --> 00:12:10.270
About how I can save Layra and 
Yuzu with my entertainment!

00:12:10.680 --> 00:12:12.490
I want to save them both.

00:12:12.490 --> 00:12:15.510
Even if people say it's impossible, 
or that they can't trust me...

00:12:15.910 --> 00:12:19.520
I want to save Yuzu and Layra, who saved me!

00:12:19.520 --> 00:12:21.220
Yuzu...

00:12:25.650 --> 00:12:28.700
I'm going to use this to become 
stronger than before.

00:12:28.700 --> 00:12:30.530
Let's go, Gongenzaka!

00:12:39.670 --> 00:12:40.960
My turn!

00:12:41.440 --> 00:12:46.090
I use the Pendulum Scale already 
set to Pendulum Summon.

00:12:46.090 --> 00:12:48.200
Be reborn from my Extra Deck,

00:12:48.200 --> 00:12:50.650
Odd-Eyes Pendulum Dragon!

00:12:53.540 --> 00:12:57.090
I activate Continuous Spell Pendulum 
Illusion from my hand!

00:12:57.090 --> 00:12:58.290
And...

00:13:01.140 --> 00:13:02.140
Battle.

00:13:02.140 --> 00:13:07.360
I attack Steam Train King with 
Odd-Eyes Pendulum Dragon!

00:13:07.670 --> 00:13:10.360
Yuya's mounted a monster in pursuit!

00:13:10.360 --> 00:13:13.500
But Steam Train King has 4800 defense points!

00:13:13.500 --> 00:13:18.780
Odd-Eyes Pendulum Dragon, with its 2500 
attack points, can't hope to compete!

00:13:18.780 --> 00:13:20.960
When a Pendulum Monster does battle,

00:13:20.960 --> 00:13:25.800
Pendulum Illusion lets me send a spell 
or trap from my field to the graveyard,

00:13:25.800 --> 00:13:27.350
to activate its effect.

00:13:27.350 --> 00:13:32.820
I send Action Spell Damage Banish to 
the graveyard, to activate its effect!

00:13:32.820 --> 00:13:34.810
During the Battle Phase,

00:13:34.810 --> 00:13:38.070
it halves one of your monsters' 
attack and defense points.

00:13:38.530 --> 00:13:41.270
Now, Steam Train King's defense 
points are down to 2400!

00:13:41.270 --> 00:13:41.900
Yes!

00:13:41.900 --> 00:13:42.530
Now...

00:13:42.530 --> 00:13:43.770
...he can destroy it!

00:13:43.770 --> 00:13:45.470
Go, Odd-Eyes.

00:13:45.960 --> 00:13:48.470
Spiral Strike Burst!

00:13:50.070 --> 00:13:53.660
A monster receiving Pendulum 
Illusion's effect isn't destroyed,

00:13:53.660 --> 00:13:55.250
but takes piercing damage.

00:13:59.340 --> 00:14:00.450
He did it!

00:14:00.750 --> 00:14:02.760
But it's only 200!

00:14:02.760 --> 00:14:04.090
Is that all he's got?

00:14:04.090 --> 00:14:05.420
It isn't that impressive.

00:14:05.420 --> 00:14:07.660
But it gives me the shivers!

00:14:07.660 --> 00:14:10.260
They're hitting each other with 
everything they have.

00:14:10.260 --> 00:14:12.860
In other words, they're evenly matched.

00:14:13.300 --> 00:14:16.970
When the battle ends, 
Pendulum Illusion's effect ends,

00:14:16.970 --> 00:14:19.470
and Steam Train King's defense 
points return to normal.

00:14:19.840 --> 00:14:21.940
I now end my turn!

00:14:22.280 --> 00:14:24.640
My turn... Draw!

00:14:24.640 --> 00:14:29.110
I applaud your determination in 
attacking me, face-to-face.

00:14:29.110 --> 00:14:31.240
Thus, I shall also attack, face-to-face.

00:14:31.240 --> 00:14:32.350
Battle!

00:14:32.350 --> 00:14:37.400
Stream Train King attacks 
Odd-Eyes Pendulum Dragon!

00:14:37.400 --> 00:14:41.160
This attack could destroy 
Odd-Eyes Pendulum Dragon!

00:14:43.010 --> 00:14:46.500
I send Action Spell Flame Guard 
from my hand to the graveyard,

00:14:46.500 --> 00:14:48.740
to activate Pendulum Illusion's effect!

00:14:49.730 --> 00:14:53.400
Now, Odd-Eyes's attack 
points are higher again!

00:14:58.950 --> 00:15:03.050
Pendulum Illusion also negates 
Steam Train King's destruction!

00:15:03.360 --> 00:15:05.250
But he takes the damage.

00:15:05.250 --> 00:15:06.750
And it's doubled!

00:15:16.080 --> 00:15:19.600
By sending two cards from 
my hand to the graveyard,

00:15:19.600 --> 00:15:21.730
Steam Train King can destroy one monster.

00:15:22.040 --> 00:15:27.070
I send Action Spell Tenacity and Superheavy 
Samurai Big Waraji to the graveyard,

00:15:27.070 --> 00:15:28.440
to activate their effects!

00:15:28.440 --> 00:15:31.530
I destroy Odd-Eyes Pendulum Dragon.

00:15:31.910 --> 00:15:37.400
Then, I banish Tenacity from my graveyard, 
to deal Yuya 200 damage!

00:15:41.850 --> 00:15:45.980
At the end of the Battle Phase, 
Pendulum Illusion's effect ends,

00:15:45.980 --> 00:15:48.460
and Steam Train King's defense 
points return to normal.

00:15:48.840 --> 00:15:51.060
I now end my turn.

00:15:54.680 --> 00:15:57.070
Each deals 200 damage again, eh?

00:15:57.070 --> 00:15:59.850
It's the straightforward sort 
of battle that Yoko likes.

00:16:00.630 --> 00:16:03.370
She'll regret leaving early.

00:16:03.370 --> 00:16:06.490
I thought about leaving, but sorry!

00:16:06.490 --> 00:16:08.840
Go for it! Go!

00:16:08.840 --> 00:16:10.350
Get him more!

00:16:13.280 --> 00:16:15.000
My turn!

00:16:15.000 --> 00:16:18.990
Continuous Spell Pendulum Illusion's 
effect prevents me from drawing.

00:16:18.990 --> 00:16:20.690
I Pendulum Summon!

00:16:20.690 --> 00:16:24.830
I call Odd-Eyes Pendulum Dragon 
back from my Extra Deck!

00:16:31.590 --> 00:16:32.640
Battle.

00:16:32.640 --> 00:16:35.310
I attack Steam Train King with Odd-Eyes!

00:16:35.310 --> 00:16:37.410
I won't let you get that Action Card!

00:16:37.410 --> 00:16:39.240
Gongenzaka's gone after it!

00:16:39.240 --> 00:16:41.010
Look out! You're gonna crash!

00:16:43.750 --> 00:16:47.790
Gongenzaka abandoned his immovable 
duel, just to encourage me.

00:16:47.790 --> 00:16:49.820
I have to meet him with everything I've got!

00:16:50.070 --> 00:16:51.800
That's right. Try harder.

00:16:51.800 --> 00:16:52.920
Come with me, Yuya.

00:16:52.920 --> 00:16:54.260
I won't let you beat me!

00:16:59.830 --> 00:17:03.130
I send Action Card Flame 
Chain to the graveyard,

00:17:03.130 --> 00:17:05.370
to activate Pendulum Illusion's effect!

00:17:09.880 --> 00:17:12.340
Spiral Strike Burst!

00:17:17.700 --> 00:17:19.640
When the Battle Phase ends,

00:17:19.640 --> 00:17:21.490
Steam Train King's defense 
points return to normal.

00:17:22.360 --> 00:17:24.220
I now end my turn!

00:17:24.590 --> 00:17:26.620
My... turn!

00:17:27.720 --> 00:17:29.390
Battle! Steam Train King!

00:17:30.860 --> 00:17:32.590
The same exchange again?

00:17:32.590 --> 00:17:34.100
How long will this go on?

00:17:35.890 --> 00:17:40.460
I send an Action Spell to the graveyard, 
to activate Pendulum Illusion's effect!

00:17:41.570 --> 00:17:44.040
But it's kind of incredible!

00:17:44.040 --> 00:17:46.280
Spiral Strike Burst!

00:17:49.190 --> 00:17:51.960
I send Action Spell Flame Surge

00:17:51.960 --> 00:17:56.320
and Superheavy Samurai Soulbeads to 
my graveyard to destroy Odd-Eyes!

00:17:58.790 --> 00:18:02.560
And I banish Flame Surge from my graveyard

00:18:02.560 --> 00:18:04.800
to deal 200 damage!

00:18:08.530 --> 00:18:11.170
Neither one is giving an inch!

00:18:11.170 --> 00:18:13.160
Pendulum Illusion's effect ends,

00:18:13.160 --> 00:18:15.140
and Steam Train King's defense 
points return to normal.

00:18:15.560 --> 00:18:18.110
And... It's my turn!

00:18:18.480 --> 00:18:22.210
I can't draw, so I use Pendulum 
Summon to call Odd-Eyes back.

00:18:27.080 --> 00:18:29.020
Battle, Odd-Eyes!

00:18:34.430 --> 00:18:35.960
It's over, this turn!

00:18:35.960 --> 00:18:37.290
I'll stop you!

00:18:58.640 --> 00:19:00.350
Damn!

00:19:00.860 --> 00:19:04.190
I send Action Spell Flame 
Surge to the graveyard,

00:19:04.190 --> 00:19:06.650
to activate Pendulum Illusion's effect!

00:19:15.110 --> 00:19:16.270
Gongenzaka?

00:19:20.980 --> 00:19:23.340
I'll take the last one, face-to-face.

00:19:24.100 --> 00:19:25.680
Come on, Yuya!

00:19:27.140 --> 00:19:29.520
Okay! Let's go, Gongenzaka!

00:19:29.520 --> 00:19:32.020
Spiral Strike Burst!

00:19:35.120 --> 00:19:38.410
Odd-Eyes's effect doubles the damage.

00:19:38.410 --> 00:19:40.620
Reaction Force!

00:19:51.270 --> 00:19:52.400
Gongenzaka!

00:19:54.040 --> 00:19:56.870
This is entertainment? Don't be ridiculous.

00:19:57.560 --> 00:20:00.470
Your entertainment should 
be much better than this.

00:20:02.860 --> 00:20:06.280
Save Yuzu and Layra, and prove that.

00:20:06.710 --> 00:20:08.020
Gongenzaka...

00:20:08.750 --> 00:20:13.510
Th-The winner is Yuya Sakaki!

00:20:21.020 --> 00:20:25.380
That means Yuya graduates 
from Junior Youth to Youth—

00:20:25.380 --> 00:20:27.840
No, I don't acknowledge that yet.

00:20:32.280 --> 00:20:36.980
I held this battle royal as a continuation 
of the Maiami Championship

00:20:36.980 --> 00:20:40.420
that Academia's invasion interrupted.

00:20:40.420 --> 00:20:42.570
At that time, the remaining duelists

00:20:42.570 --> 00:20:45.610
were those that were chosen as Lancers.

00:20:46.200 --> 00:20:50.010
Among them, only the last one 
standing could advance to Youth.

00:20:50.490 --> 00:20:54.930
Yuya, that means there are 
others you must beat.

00:20:55.680 --> 00:20:57.380
Others I must beat...

00:21:02.280 --> 00:21:03.480
What is this?

00:21:03.480 --> 00:21:05.390
A gate to the dimensional route.

00:21:05.390 --> 00:21:06.840
Dimensional route?

00:21:07.110 --> 00:21:10.490
I told you that the world was divided 
into four dimensions again,

00:21:10.490 --> 00:21:13.940
but the truth is that ARC-V's 
remnants are at their center.

00:21:14.320 --> 00:21:18.990
ARC-V and the four dimensions 
are connected by wormholes,

00:21:18.990 --> 00:21:21.660
which we call the dimensional route.

00:21:21.660 --> 00:21:25.500
You need to go to the Xyz Dimension.

00:21:25.760 --> 00:21:29.700
Xyz? You want me to fight Kurosaki?

00:21:30.040 --> 00:21:31.190
Isn't that right?

00:21:31.190 --> 00:21:35.540
The remaining Lancers are 
Serena, Kurosaki, and Dennis.

00:21:36.400 --> 00:21:40.730
But Serena was sent into 
ARC-V with the others...

00:21:41.280 --> 00:21:46.820
Saving Yuzu probably means saving 
Serena, Ruri, and Rin.

00:21:46.820 --> 00:21:48.750
If dueling is the only way to do that,

00:21:49.270 --> 00:21:51.550
I'll fight anyone it takes.

00:21:51.550 --> 00:21:53.220
And I'll win!

00:21:56.490 --> 00:21:58.010
I made a vow

00:21:58.010 --> 00:22:00.400
that I would save the world 
with entertainment.

00:22:00.760 --> 00:22:02.090
Let's go, Kurosaki.

00:22:02.090 --> 00:22:03.190
I'm waiting!

00:22:07.940 --> 00:22:09.070
That's...

00:23:49.560 --> 00:23:51.340
I've been waiting, Yuya.

00:23:51.340 --> 00:23:53.400
Dennis! What are you doing here?

00:23:53.400 --> 00:23:55.930
Obviously, I'm here to fight you.

00:23:55.930 --> 00:23:57.080
Fight me?

00:23:57.080 --> 00:23:58.170
But this is...

00:23:58.170 --> 00:23:59.680
Kurosaki isn't here.

00:23:59.680 --> 00:24:02.380
He went to the Fusion Dimension...

00:24:02.380 --> 00:24:05.460
But if you want to follow him, 
you'll have to beat me.

00:24:05.460 --> 00:24:08.580
Though, I have no intention of losing.

00:24:09.890 --> 00:24:14.190
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ARC-V: 
The Cursed Gear Mask.

00:24:14.190 --> 00:24:16.190
The fun is only getting started!
